                    {
                        "form_id": "e1e27396-206d-45f7-a713-c53678b1b3bc",
                        "entry_id": "b4e6cd65-f368-3e71-a520-2d5ce49ce3c6",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "short-form"
                        ],
                        "form": "бессла́вны"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c32a78a5-a046-3602-befd-143113d62a9c",
                        "entry_id": "b4e6cd65-f368-3e71-a520-2d5ce49ce3c6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "не заслуживающий славы, уважения; недостойный, позорный"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "59b721ed-3d7d-4826-9b00-aa8aeedeec05",
                                "sense_id": "c32a78a5-a046-3602-befd-143113d62a9c",
                                "text": "― Помнишь ли, пустой, пустой, бесславный, малодушный, вечно, вечно пустой человек!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7c25734d-2d12-47e7-b94b-4d983d78784f",
                                "sense_id": "c32a78a5-a046-3602-befd-143113d62a9c",
                                "text": "Что ж, их ждет та же участь, тот же бесславный конец, что и их бесноватого предшественника…"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ca10acbc-3960-4928-be51-30d0dd430f3a",
                        "source_entry_id": "b4e6cd65-f368-3e71-a520-2d5ce49ce3c6",
                        "source_sense_id": "c32a78a5-a046-3602-befd-143113d62a9c",
                        "target_lang_word": "inglorious",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "inglorious",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "490c6681-4cd6-3854-ba75-de32c45fd9de",
                                        "entry_id": "6a722eb3-7eb8-31ed-a802-7729e11531d3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ignominious; disgraceful."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1cc7868d-11ed-4734-88c4-30e4c413c29e",
                                                "sense_id": "490c6681-4cd6-3854-ba75-de32c45fd9de",
                                                "text": "Oh inglorious league: / Shall we vpon the footing of our land, / Send fayre-play-orders, and make comprimiſe, / Inſinuation, parley, and baſe truce / To Armes Inuaſiue?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "febfb23c-942e-4a13-a9b4-175e41ad56aa",
                                                "sense_id": "490c6681-4cd6-3854-ba75-de32c45fd9de",
                                                "text": "Resolved to pursue no inglorious career, he turned his eyes toward the East, as affording scope for his spirit of enterprise."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cc2b5869-dd25-44aa-a1cd-3f237ed7af3a",
                                                "sense_id": "490c6681-4cd6-3854-ba75-de32c45fd9de",
                                                "text": "[H]e cast about in his mind for a way to beat a retreat not too inglorious."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f7b65342-534c-4ac9-bd91-9f04a960e61c",
                                                "sense_id": "490c6681-4cd6-3854-ba75-de32c45fd9de",
                                                "text": "The last occasion on which the Kaiser [Wilhelm II] used this train was for an inglorious journey into Holland towards the end of the 1914 war. He spent the night in it at Eysden [Eijsden], while the Queen of the Netherlands and a hastily summoned Cabinet debated what to do with him."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d0c95bdd-d92d-3f65-b114-81d5c1d9fa93",
                                        "entry_id": "6a722eb3-7eb8-31ed-a802-7729e11531d3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Not famous; obscure."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6797807b-251a-4b09-94a0-9ce410fc9ed1",
                                                "sense_id": "d0c95bdd-d92d-3f65-b114-81d5c1d9fa93",
                                                "text": "Great Julius [Caesar], whom now all the world admires / The more he grew in years, the more inflam’d / With glory, wept that he had liv’d ſo long / Inglorious: but thou yet art not too late."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "59a80f36-b293-447f-81b6-35fd0c6bd479",
                        "source_entry_id": "b4e6cd65-f368-3e71-a520-2d5ce49ce3c6",
                        "source_sense_id": "c32a78a5-a046-3602-befd-143113d62a9c",
                        "target_lang_word": "infamous",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "infamous",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cf730dcd-cd60-3899-84fa-d8a317223ad6",
                                        "entry_id": "489fb079-e037-3ab9-9d27-6e5be2fbc35b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having a bad reputation; disreputable; notorious; unpleasant or evil; widely known, especially for something scornful."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b2b5edbd-0019-4fce-8ec7-ade587392f6e",
                                                "sense_id": "cf730dcd-cd60-3899-84fa-d8a317223ad6",
                                                "text": "He was an infamous traitor."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de6e93d8-5806-489b-8438-c9e8a805496e",
                                                "sense_id": "cf730dcd-cd60-3899-84fa-d8a317223ad6",
                                                "text": "She is infamous for perjury."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3d8b3f08-23e4-4d89-a8ea-534f3f5345d5",
                                                "sense_id": "cf730dcd-cd60-3899-84fa-d8a317223ad6",
                                                "text": "Soon we arrived at the Beijing Hotel—within shouting distance of the now infamous Tienanmen Square."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "da3a1c6a-e84a-47fc-873a-f4a01500a861",
                                                "sense_id": "cf730dcd-cd60-3899-84fa-d8a317223ad6",
                                                "text": "These infamous little green men appeared during the decisive seizures or buildings and facilities, only to disappear when associated militias and local troops arrived to consolidate the gains. In this way they provided a measure of deniability—however superficial or implausible—for Moscow.⁴⁰"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "72d3bb79-a713-4b86-b009-3a7054f5e80d",
                                                "sense_id": "cf730dcd-cd60-3899-84fa-d8a317223ad6",
                                                "text": "Despite the line proving to be a useful strategic route for men and supplies to the British naval fleets stationed at Scapa Flow in both world wars, the Duke's legacy looked to have passed into history when it was listed for closure in the infamous Beeching report."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a640466b-714e-38c8-b422-96d5a8c35475",
                                        "entry_id": "489fb079-e037-3ab9-9d27-6e5be2fbc35b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Causing infamy; disgraceful."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "857a40a3-567d-4c09-8a5f-b1b397fb83e8",
                                                "sense_id": "a640466b-714e-38c8-b422-96d5a8c35475",
                                                "text": "This infamous deed tarnishes all involved."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3ea915f0-c9ab-445b-bdd2-eb7074512f9e",
                                                "sense_id": "a640466b-714e-38c8-b422-96d5a8c35475",
                                                "text": "Yes, Virginia, now Santa's doin' time\nIn a Federal prison for his infamous crime"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bef36cb5-b1dc-3e08-8d5d-054a1f33273c",
                                        "entry_id": "489fb079-e037-3ab9-9d27-6e5be2fbc35b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Subject to a judicial punishment depriving (the person) of certain rights (e.g. the rights to hold public office, exercise the franchise, receive a public pension, serve on a jury, or give testimony in a court of law)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e8c2c682-fc6b-363b-9595-8ad78fb4d318",
                                        "entry_id": "489fb079-e037-3ab9-9d27-6e5be2fbc35b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Punishable by death or imprisonment."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5423b4b1-0088-4b7e-92a3-f039bf580043",
                                                "sense_id": "e8c2c682-fc6b-363b-9595-8ad78fb4d318",
                                                "text": "No person shall be held to answer for a capital, or otherwise infamous crime, unless on a presentment or indictment of a Grand Jury, except in cases arising in the land or naval forces, or in the Militia, when in actual service in time of war or public danger […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c4096d61-4e43-4ca6-8826-182072b1b9f0",
                        "source_entry_id": "b4e6cd65-f368-3e71-a520-2d5ce49ce3c6",
